matt reeves of batman is everywhere  right now the first batman solo movie in  10 years made more than 164 million  dollars at the american box office just  six days into its theatrical run and  according to box office mojo it's  already the second highest grossing film  of 2022 in the batman robert pattinson's  batman has been patrolling gotham city  streets at night for nearly two years  with little to show for it his fledgling  partnership with police lieutenant james  gordon leaves a tour at odds with the  rest of the city's power structure and  it all comes to head when the riddler  starts killing gotham politicians paul  dano's depiction of the riddler was the  first time the character appears in big  screen live-action batman content since  jim carrey played the role in 1995's  batman forever it's a distinctly  different approach daniel's character  appears much more like a villain in a  serial killer movie than carrie's loud  bombastic trickster the batman also  includes villains the penguin and  carmine falcone but perhaps the most  intriguing villain is one who makes only  an uncredited cameo appearance at the  end of the film spoilers ahead  barry kyogen of eternals and the killing  of a sacred deer fame is only credited  as unseen arkham prisoner and the batman  but when he appears imprisoned alongside  the riddler at the end of the movie  nobody could mistake him for batman's  arch nemesis the joker reeves attempts  to set up a litany of batman villains  for his burgeoning cinematic universe in  fact a deleted scene reportedly shows  batman visiting kyogen in prison to get  a profile on the riddler which has fans  wondering what the actor would be like  as the clown prince of crime while  reeves has said these villains are in  their infancy in the batman it seems  pretty clear kyogen's character will  take on the joker title in whatever  future sequel awaits robert pattinson's  batman in the meantime fans like  instagram user refinity are offering up  sample art of what kyogen's joker could  look like with green hair clown makeup  and an exaggerated red smile behind  kyogen's joker is graffiti similar to  what is seen in the batman but joker  themed kyogen's prison jumpsuit sports  the name joe although it's unclear what  reeve's joker real name is as of yet  reeves told ign that his conception of  kyogin's pre-joker stage involves a  character having a condition that makes  it impossible for him to stop smiling  making his joker title a reflection of  having lived life as a cruel joke  however the director stressed that  kyogen's inclusion is not necessarily  meant to tease the joker as a villain  for his next movie reeves told ign i  don't know that the joker would be in  the next movie but i can tell you that  here's what you're seeing is an early  days version of this character and  trouble as always is brewing in gotham  for the most part fans are liking the  potential they see in a new kind of  joker instagram user refinity said they  enjoyed the batman in the instagram post  containing their interpretation of how  kyogen's joker could look complementing  the film's portrayal of batman as a  detective and the effects posting the  visuals were stunning and most of it  looked practical which i appreciate cast  chemistry was great paul dana was  probably my favorite out of the cast  that one scene if you know you know was  exceptional reactions to the users joker  fanart which positions the right half of  pattinson's batman opposite the left  half of kyogen as the joker emphasizing  the yin-yang nature of their  relationship appear positive plenty of  users left fire emojis in the comments  of the post and the word epic was tossed  around one user wrote love this i wasn't  so sure of barry playing the joker but  when i saw it his laugh stole the show  audiences don't see much of kyogen at  all in his one scene but once his  character establishes a budding  friendship with dano's riddler that's a  mistakeable laugh signals plenty of  trouble ahead for pattinson's bruce  wayne  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the batman are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one
 

